write('blueprint','# Domain 5 final assessment blueprint\n\n40 original slots; **38 retained** after independent semantic review excluded1003/1025. All26 curated families retained. Initial50 reduced to40 for distinct decisions, then38 for demonstrated overlap. No quantity target overrides quality.\n\nFinal distributions: `'+json.dumps(counts)+'`. Difficulty and cognitive labels are conservative editorial judgments, not learner-calibrated statistics or ISC2 quotas. A recognition;B distinction;C application;D evidence interpretation;E action under constraints.\n\nCanonical English plus equivalent auxiliary Thai fields. Metadata is excluded from the11-field runtime. `blueprint.json` preserves all40 slots including exclusions.\n\n| ID | Objective/family | Knowledge | Cognitive/difficulty/type | Assessed decision |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n'+'\n'.join(f"| {d['id']} | {d['objective']}/{d['family']} | {d['knowledge']} | {d['cognitive']}/{d['difficulty']}/{d['stemType']} | {d['assessedDecision']} |" for d in good))
write('coverage','# Domain 5 final objective coverage\n\nBased on the dated official outline R01 printedp7. Five objectives and14 bullet groups; local family codes are editorial, not official subobjective IDs. Original historical coverage report is unchanged.\n\n| Objective | Retained IDs | Curated families |\n|---|---|---|\n'+'\n'.join(f"| {obj} | {', '.join(str(d['id']) for d in good if d['objective']==obj)} | {', '.join(sorted({d['family'] for d in good if d['objective']==obj}))} |" for obj in ['5.1','5.2','5.3','5.4','5.5'])+'\n\n| Bullet group (paraphrase) | Assessment evidence |\n|---|---|\n| Data handling |1001/1002 category and marking;1004 masking limitation/AI sharing;1005/1006 sanitization|\n| Cryptographic examples |1007 public-key role;1008 trusted digest;1009/1010 PQC; shared-secret/signature distinctions taught in KNOW-D5-004, not separate recall items|\n| Logging/monitoring |1011/1012|\n| Triage/use cases/priority/correlation |1013–1016|\n| Actors/motivation |1017 deliberate versus accidental insider|\n| Threat intelligence |1018/1019|\n| Frameworks |1020 goal versus method|\n| IR plan/data policy |1021/1022 protected sharing/hold;1023/1024 authorized containment/recovery|\n| Exercises |1026 discussion versus demonstrated operational capability;1025 excluded as duplicate|\n| Lifecycle/EOL |1027–1029|\n| Configuration/change |1030–1032|\n| Team readiness |1033/1034; red/blue/purple compared under stated activities|\n| Application assessment |1035–1038 scan limits/static/runtime/modeling|\n| Physical examples |1039/1040 distinguishes electronic phishing, entry following, identity pretext and work-order verification|\n\nCoverage means distinct introductory decisions supported by curated knowledge. It does not mean every algorithm, actor category, lifecycle phase, example or source fact has its own question. No claims about confidential exam frequency. AllHigh findings resolved/qualified/excluded in remediation ledger; F19 crop/provenance limits and excluded hardware/legal claims remain disclosed.')
write('duplicates','# Domain 5 duplicate and ambiguity review\n\nCompared all40 initial candidates against702 existing stems/correct answers and within the batch using ranked lexical candidates plus manual semantic adjudication. Exact normalized EN/TH stem checks also executed in the integration verifier. Lexical similarity is a retrieval aid, not acceptance proof. Full existing distractor/rationale audit is not claimed.\n\n**Rejected1003:** same masking-recognition decision and last-four support context as updated585. **Rejected1025:** same discussion-only tabletop selection as updated638 and legacy197/417. Neither exported. IDs retained in history and not recycled.\n\n**Kept1016:** cross-event correlation lacks shared account/host/session linkage; distinct from668/701 single-event anomaly triage. Other pair decisions are item-specific in independent-review.json (`semanticComparators`,`duplicateVerdict`).\n\nPotential neighboring learning pairs1001/1002,1005/1027,1011/1012,1033/1034,1036/1037 were examined: each changes the assessed decision (category distinction/rule use; sanitization/lifecycle release; purpose/source selection; collaboration/gap retest; nonexecuting/runtime evidence). Shared foundations can aid practice; these are not statistically independent calibrated exam items. Existing sampler is unchanged and no form-level independence claim is made.\n\nInitial blind solve40/40 agreement. Revision3 changed distractors and1032 mandatory rollback condition received focused independent re-solving. Authority/timing/policy supplied in items1014,1021–1024,1029–1032,1040. No numerical score rescues an ambiguous item. Review preserves initial defects and repair history.')
write('authoring-manifest','# Domain 5 authoring manifest\n\nCanonical machine-readable manifest: `content/isc2-cc-2026/sources/domain-5/production/authoring-manifest.json`. It retains40 IDs,26 family/knowledge mappings, final cognitive/difficulty/type labels, misconception and ambiguity controls, actual local paths/line ranges/hashes, references, revision and rejected status. Draft master: `drafts.json`; four batch JSONs are initial historical inputs and are not the accepted source of truth.\n\nExporter: `content/isc2-cc-2026/questions/domain-5-draft.mjs`. Staged runtime objects have exact11 existing fields, integer identifiers, dom5, zero-based keys,4 EN/TH options and mapped bilingual correct/incorrect feedback. No editorial metadata is published. Keys were assigned in original authoring seed20261103; exclusions explain gaps and final answer distribution.\n\nReference register includes R26 RFC8017§5.1 public/private encryption primitives, R27 Microsoft Service Assurance joint red/blue purple exercises, R28 NIST80084§5 operational exercises. Source texts and audit reports are unchanged. No protected exam, dump or embedded source quiz was copied.')
